WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.677
CASE and FILTER are two styles for conditional aggregation.

00:00:03.677 --> 00:00:06.682
CASE is broadly portable and flexible.

00:00:06.682 --> 00:00:13.112
FILTER is particularly readable in PostgreSQL when you want category-specific counts or sums.

00:00:13.112 --> 00:00:17.562
Choose the form that is clear for the environment you are using.

00:00:17.562 --> 00:00:22.912
The output grain and aggregate meaning matter more than the stylistic choice.

00:00:22.912 --> 00:00:30.862
A pivot converts category values into columns, usually through conditional aggregation in portable SQL.

00:00:30.862 --> 00:00:34.692
Each target column needs a clear aggregation rule.

00:00:34.692 --> 00:00:40.082
Before pivoting, check whether the source contains more than one value for the same row-key and category

00:00:40.082 --> 00:00:41.440
combination.
